{"title":"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Very_similar_to_Solution_1)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Very similar to Solution 1)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Visualization_Tip\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Visualization Tip</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/9/8c9b0ce39d9464fbfd62e0923a3751ec3ca8c0f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1A_2\\dots A_{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"99\" height=\"17\" /> be a non-convex <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />-gon such that\n</p><p>• The area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/3/ad33336d982493eb3a6eeda8e5725ece8f16a517.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_iA_1A_{i+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/2/802e0235d81ec9ddef32acce704e5d067c22a14b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\le i \\le 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"81\" height=\"15\" />,\n</p><p>• <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/4/cb4065828025815ad49c6bfca3c55d01fce5200c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(\\angle A_iA_1A_{i+1})=\\frac{12}{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"176\" height=\"38\" /> for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/2/802e0235d81ec9ddef32acce704e5d067c22a14b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\le i \\le 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"81\" height=\"15\" />,\n</p><p>• The perimeter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/9/8c9b0ce39d9464fbfd62e0923a3751ec3ca8c0f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1A_2\\dots A_{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"99\" height=\"17\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/2/b32c732cc6aa45c42c79689d105dbda183449d39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1A_2+A_1A_{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"17\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/4/db48b2a986b6cf0bed8550783e3d3e58b4adf1d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m\\sqrt{n}-p}{q}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"79\" height=\"45\" /> for positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/e/5aec0a3b6296e5f63052d09c8e9a5454f42b7681.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m,n,p,q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"13\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> squarefree and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/5/a8597b5d7fb65f988eed956da25a9eb2abb783c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gcd(m,p,q)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"127\" height=\"20\" />, find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/0/740b7804fdc9546a926406b6b1e2b10490f85a06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n+p+q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"111\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/4/7d4c6f2ddbd26551c3ed05ad7648f9d0cec49f0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1A_2 = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/b/72bab51575d9c816ebf32ff0f67c02db88c3ee61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1A_3 = y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" />. By the first condition, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/9/829bb3e5911517d5e190d2623c626a69ddd8cfdc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}xy\\sin\\theta = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"106\" height=\"38\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/3/1938074de30e1eb7e2b0c81dfac305afeeeff25b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta = \\angle A_2 A_1 A_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"111\" height=\"17\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/7/2a7f9309d9bfee3fbd77883754922a95f206d3c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos\\theta = \\frac{12}{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"85\" height=\"38\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/7/877b22f68b941b699f96c7daf51b5ecba2ede16a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin\\theta = \\frac{5}{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"83\" height=\"38\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/0/f707cdcf2fae26cd01a14426c3ca38282f795f84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy = \\frac{26}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"68\" height=\"38\" />. Repeating this process for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/e/87e7ecef6f285f045c640582598c6d57de83ccc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle A_i A_1 A_{i+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"94\" height=\"18\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/e/07ed04a8dda3271401e3a685fa6e9aec807f5cea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1A_2 = A_1A_4 = \\ldots A_1A_{10} = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"242\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/8/328d38623420be50dbda142c7445fd45624e0e76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1A_3 = A_1A_5 = \\ldots A_1A_{11} = y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"241\" height=\"18\" />. Since the included angle of these <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> triangles is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the square of the third side is \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/8/908507a40f8b18f446da8709d556907ae616f546.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2 + y^2 - 2xy\\cos\\theta = x^2 + y^2 - \\frac{52}{5}\\cdot \\frac{12}{13} = x^2 + y^2 - \\frac{48}{5} = (x+y)^2 - 20.\\]\" width=\"537\" height=\"38\" />\nThus the third side has length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/f/81f0da077a82282ef5307c5e645ae1f30d373beb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{(x+y)^2 - 20}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"129\" height=\"35\" /> The perimeter is constructed from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of these lengths, plus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/4/074fabc4b5107f000718f0e7c9cfdbcc369fb2f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{11}A_1 + A_1A_2 = x + y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"181\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/b/81b13d187496404870088b2728d38c6442143009.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9\\sqrt{(x+y)^2 - 20} + x + y = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"240\" height=\"35\" />. We seek the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/8/4680df10669c3792645baa652d41f394d1195d45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + y,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> so let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/f/82f241088a4fb7487a2c5864d913d8361d0c6610.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + y = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"76\" height=\"14\" /> so \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/b/3eb30dee841c37e189220666553d22c075b7aa03.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 9\\sqrt{a^2 - 20} + a &amp;= 20\\\\ 81(a^2 - 20) &amp;= 400 - 40a + a^2\\\\ 4a^2 + 2a - 101 &amp;= 0 \\\\ a &amp;= \\frac{-2 \\pm \\sqrt{1620}}{8} = \\frac{-1 \\pm \\sqrt{405}}{4} = \\frac{-1 \\pm 9\\sqrt{5}}{4}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"468\" height=\"125\" />\nTaking the positive solution gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/7/587101e259cbd2d7eea3cc9f4cbdf6ef1e3d8c7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m + n + p + q = 1 + 9 + 5 + 4 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(019)}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"325\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>-Benedict T (countmath1)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Very_similar_to_Solution_1.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Very_similar_to_Solution_1)\">Solution 2 (Very similar to Solution 1)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Very similar to Solution 1)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/4/d94bafbd814d5969a39c7b6b360a9c0ff5b6f081.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1 A_2 = a_1, A_1 A_3 = a_2, ... A_1 A_{10} = a_9, A_1 A_11 a_{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"373\" height=\"18\" />. Now the area of each triangle is equal to half the product of two side lengths and the sine of the angle in between. This angle's cosine is given to us to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/a/14aeefc3d3435fc2484af58aa32401c9ce8683f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{12}{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />. We recognize this as a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c1645fea006e40422df8465ad25c74bc33e615eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5-12-13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"15\" /> triangle hence the sine of the angle will be simply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/5/04507e0fa21b60025a05bfc5e52f460e7915baac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" /> (alternatively, one could use the Pythagorean Identity <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/0/700b53ca266c77f8c88f49120ba26850769dc0af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin^2(\\angle A_iA_1A_{i+1})+\\cos^2(\\angle A_iA_1A_{i+1})=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"325\" height=\"22\" />). Hence each area will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/6/8265afcfbd2d78dffd1543bfe1bee4563a038f87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot a_n a_{n + 1} \\cdot \\frac{5}{13} = 1 \\implies a_n a_{n+ 1} = \\frac{26}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"301\" height=\"38\" />. Therefore, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/6/e56a49390f20b984bf43ef44f8971d3fefe7e787.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 a_2 = \\frac{26}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"82\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/2/7d203a82b78e90e0cdf80654ff4ee560707d62d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2 a_3 = \\frac{26}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"82\" height=\"38\" />\n.\n.\n.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/e/32e6d702a98f5a968da5848423e53edd23236129.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_9 a_{10} = \\frac{26}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"89\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/1/1f1857f2e56b3be01e1ddf42c875f1f88966b9df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{10} a_1 = \\frac{26}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"89\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Now note that the perimeter is the sum of all the other lengths. For instance, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/4/5d41968388f29cc1a6a40b12218912d4b9b04de6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_2 A_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" /> will be part of this perimeter which happens to be the only unknown side of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/7/a57552814ae47aeaeca907ea974fbd2f1366b66f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle A_1 A_2 A_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"18\" />. By Law of Cosines\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/1/f4187243ec473deda8897308673b63b63ce957b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(A_2 A_3)^2 = a_1^{2} + a_2^{2} - 2a_1 a_2 \\frac{12}{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"234\" height=\"38\" /> after substituting the cosine value. We know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/6/e56a49390f20b984bf43ef44f8971d3fefe7e787.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 a_2 = \\frac{26}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"82\" height=\"38\" /> so substituting this in we get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/7/5a79c5e9d80c189aa33d6cb65db8539eb2ba4b90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(A_2 A_3)^2 = a_1^{2} + a_2^{2} - \\frac{48}{5} \\implies A_2 A_3 = \\sqrt{a_1^{2} + a_2^{2} - \\frac{48}{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"425\" height=\"45\" />. By symmetry, we conclude\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/3/1b3c63a47623d893817ea5445ff8449b2332bf87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{a_1^{2} + a_2^{2} - \\frac{48}{5}} + ... + \\sqrt{a_{10}^{2} + a_1^{2} - \\frac{48}{5}} + a_1 + a_2 = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"426\" height=\"45\" /> because we need to account for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/d/ebd6fd0603a1b97aa678289a70e604a129625ea7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1 A_2 + A_1 A_{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"17\" /> as they are actually known sides that are included in the perimeter.\n</p><p>Note that from the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/6/e56a49390f20b984bf43ef44f8971d3fefe7e787.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 a_2 = \\frac{26}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"82\" height=\"38\" /> system of equations, we can see clearly that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/0/7305e7cf8203ab169dc1961e0455f9b68a5a008d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 = a_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/2/b8229122c972bf22097353af4e6c1e9c5fc29a40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2 = a_4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />\n.\n.\n.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/6/586a347e25719a2b9e9d94b7d27833fd760cd5aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_8 = a_{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/7/0d72bebe1dedb398e0a0561f0023b452dd03b6e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_9 = a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/b/95bbbe83d44308917c325c80d616c0d86517cf06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{10} = a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>So we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/f/4dfbc644d036a12c10c4d6afe8ecac251e61f527.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2n + 1} = a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"85\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/5/11587e2761630cd9be78e7ecf5a3b8d42825b12b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2n} = a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"13\" /> so we can substitute this in to get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/3/ca328fbe3adceab7ec8e5e6ff6425c7128edbe2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{a_1^{2} + a_2^{2} - \\frac{48}{5}} + ... + \\sqrt{a_1^{2} + a_2^{2} - \\frac{48}{5}} + a_1 + a_2 = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"419\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Now the square root terms happen <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times as there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> sides and two of them are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/7/8672844162eb1e10b48e85f86caa76057dc34679.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"11\" /> given at the end of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/c/17c924be2d96aaeaadfdfd4b35b06d2a60edb5d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$LHS$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />. So we conclude:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/b/8ebda326c0cc0c8a01abe53b8f6291a8c3dc470f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9\\sqrt{a_1^{2} + a_2^{2} - \\frac{48}{5}} + a_1 + a_2 = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"250\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/d/c3d7f932fc87e28c062305dcb4b25cb25f0fbeb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1^{2} + a_2^{2} - \\frac{48}{5} = (a_1 + a_2)^2 - 2a_1 a_2 - \\frac{48}{5} = (a_1 + a_2)^2 - \\frac{52 + 48}{5} = (a_1 + a_2)^2 - 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"644\" height=\"38\" />. Note that we want to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/d/47d100400b2d69eb62bf7cf6cc803620405d7433.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1 A_2 + A_1 A_{11} = a_1 + a_{10} = a_1 + a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"283\" height=\"17\" />. So we let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/3/e23f92c4d5554b5fa0712c8fc838ce1618a8c025.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 + a_2 = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"93\" height=\"15\" /> to get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/a/91a400ce6926e945526e271c2887b2a1b046199c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[9\\sqrt{x^2 - 20} + x = 20 \\implies 81(x^2 - 20) = (20 - x)^2 \\implies 81(x^2 - 20) = 400 - 40x + x^2 \\implies 81x^2 - 1620 = 400 - 40x + x^2 \\implies 80x^2 + 40x - 2020 = 0 \\implies 4x^2 + 2x - 101 = 0 \\implies x = \\frac{-1 \\pm 9\\sqrt{5}}{4}\\]\" width=\"1452\" height=\"41\" />\nNow take the positive value to get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/b/dcb2d0435d4475c4366e7f80b74786cfbad50be2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{9\\sqrt{5} - 1}{4} \\implies 9 + 5 + 1 + 4 = \\boxed{19}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"311\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p>~ilikemath24736\n</p><p>~Sylesh (Latex errors)\n</p><p>~ Clarifying and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/latex.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\LaTeX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" /> edits by Christian\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Visualization_Tip\">Visualization Tip</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Visualization Tip\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The polygon can be imagined sort of like one of those Chinese fans. Congruent triangles branch out from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36c7f3f828cf12ab9cafeffad282468a95219600.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" />, the handle of the fan, forming a series of triangular ridges.\n</p><p>~ Christian\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II\" title=\"2025 AIME II\">2025 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2025 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2025\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2025 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017042000\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.049 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.146 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 451/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1810/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 132/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 14887/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.229      1 -total\n 59.26%    7.839      1 Template:AIME_box\n 38.95%    5.153      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pca